Z||000000||BAM-BAM||05-10-2000||08:43 PM||||   Found an 86 4cyl. and the guy wants $500.00. I've been watching it for some time now, just sitting. Called the guys business and asked how much he would want for it. He said that he had taken it in trade for some mechanic work and that it ran when he parked it. Said that it probably needs a battery(and then some). But, I figure it would at least be a good parts car. I'll find more out about it when I can get back down there. I believe he said it was a four speed 4cyl with a sunroof and 65,000 miles. It's a gold coupe with custom Centerline rims. That's about all I know at this time. What do ya think, is that a fair price? Let me know. I was going to offer him $350.00 cash. After all, he said anything he had was for sale, if he had an old lady he'd probly sell her too.<P>  Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||05-10-2000||10:33 PM||||BUY THE CAR - GRAB THE WHEELS! THEY ARE WORTH THAT MUCH BY THEMSELVES!||||reg||4
Z||000002||mrfiero||05-11-2000||02:15 AM||||I agree.  It's worth the price, if only for the wheels. <P>I just bought an '84 Fiero for $300.....I have no desire to own another '84 coupe, but it came with '88 GT wheels!!  Well worth the expense.  I'll just remove said wheels and install a set of "regular" 14" alloys and re-sell the car.  I figure I will at least get a free set of GT wheels out of the whole deal.  Not bad. ||||reg||6
Z||000003||Jay||05-11-2000||08:48 AM||||If you think that's good, I bought my 86GT three years ago for $500.  Mind you if you saw the car you'd say $500 was too much.  After a walk in the wrecking yard I pulled a new hood for $50 which was already black.  The interior was totally re-done in custom black and red and a little bit of wax, okay alot of wax and she looks like a million bucks!  After two years the engine went, so hence enter Northstar.  My advice, buy the car!!!!  With a little bit of work you can turn around and sell it  for much more then $350 bucks!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||05-11-2000||09:16 AM||||I paid $350 for the Grape Ape.  True, the motor was shot, but it really wasn't in bad shape for 110,000 miles and the fact that it was obviously owned by a Non-Fiero loving jer-k.  $1500 later and she should be up and running (maybe even today!!!!!!!!!!!!).  Brand new Pirelli tires and ARE rims.  Those alone are probably worth a grand (that would equal about $12.38CDN).  Custom paint (seen better days) and a good wing, etc.  Buy it before I do! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||05-11-2000||11:26 AM||||Bam-Bam, assuming that Fiero is unwrecked and complete, it sounds like a good deal at $500 - every dollar you pay less than that is icing on the cake.  I wouldn't part out a complete car with only 65K miles on it - I bet someone would give you at least $2K for it in running condition.  Hell, fix it and drive it as a beater - we live in a world of $9500 Metros and $11K Daewoos.<P>Incidentally, I'm really jealous of you guys and your great deals.  Here's my Fiero-buying history...<BR>$2400 - 1984 Coupe, purchased in 1992, 74K miles, loaded, EC, needed new plugs and wires<BR>$2500 - 1988 Coupe, purchased in 1996, 68K miles, no options, EC, needed tires, shocks & struts (and a clutch, which I didn't know at the time)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>$700 - 1986 V6 SE, purchased in 1998, 117K miles, only option was A/C, needed alternator, front wheel bearings, door skin, 1/4 window, lots of trim pieces, taillamp assembly, shocks, struts, and front-end work<P>Note there are no earth-shattering deals here...||||reg||1
Z||000006||BAM-BAM||05-11-2000||11:42 PM||||   Thanks to all. You have convinced me, I will, I will, I will. I have only one  problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">The guys  closes shop at 12:30 PM and I work 6 days 6:00 AM - 4:30 PM. Should be getting a couple of Mondays off here in about three weeks. He told me it wasn't going anywhere; nobody has asked about it since he has owned it. So, patience is a virtue? I hope so <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> Thanx again, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
